\section{Introduction}
\subsection{Purpose of the Laboratory Manual}
This manual provides a complete multi-experiment framework for the
Trichological Cycle Engine (TCE), including theoretical foundations,
experimental procedures, stress-testing protocols, stability analysis,
and sovereign recovery operations. The goal is to establish a rigorous,
repeatable, and mathematically grounded methodology for evaluating
autonomous biological simulation engines.

\subsection{System Overview}
The TCE models the hair-follicle lifecycle using a hybrid dynamical
system composed of:
\begin{itemize}
    \item continuous vitality dynamics $F(t)$ governed by differential equations,
    \item discrete biological phases $\sigma(t)\in\{A,C,T\}$ representing lifecycle states,
    \item stochastic forcing $\Delta S(t)$ modeling environmental and metabolic variance,
    \item sovereign supervisory kernel $\mathcal{P}_{\text{sov}}$ providing autonomous recovery.
\end{itemize}
The system is designed for long-duration autonomous operation under
nominal, stressed, and stochastic conditions.

